TI  - Confirmed Treponema pallidum pleural effusion in patient with known syphilis.
PG  - e70069
LID - 10.1002/rcr2.70069 [doi]
LID - e70069
AB  - Pulmonary and pleural involvement in Treponema pallidum infection is uncommon. 
      Previously reported syphilis-related pleural effusions have been described 
      largely based on clinical features combined with positive syphilis serology 
      rather than the detection of T pallidum in pleural fluid or pleural biopsy. We 
      report a case of secondary syphilis and confirmed syphilitic pleural effusion via 
      thoracentesis.
