JID - 101665030
PMC - PMC12439548
OAB - Chylothorax is a rare condition where a milky fluid called chyle collects around 
      the lungs. It usually happens because of injury, cancer, or blockage of a tube in 
      the chest called the thoracic duct, which carries lymph fluid through the chest. 
      In this report, we describe a 53-year-old woman who developed chylothorax about a 
      month after having COVID-19. She came to the hospital with a persistent dry 
      cough. Tests showed fluid around her left lung, and further analysis confirmed it 
      was chyle. This case suggests that COVID-19 may, in rare cases, lead to 
      chylothorax possibly due to inflammation damaging the lymphatic system without 
      any blood clots or blocked veins. Doctors should be aware of this potential 
      complication when a patient has unexplained fluid around the lungs after 
      COVID-19.
