TI  - Utility of beta-human chorionic gonadotropin in pleural effusions: Report of an 
      autopsy case of a male patient with primary pulmonary choriocarcinoma.
PG  - e6663
LID - 10.1002/ccr3.6663 [doi]
LID - e6663
AB  - A 69-year-old male patient presented with bloody pleural fluid effusion and 
      elevated beta-human chorionic gonadotropin (β-hCG) levels obtained by 
      thoracentesis. The patient's condition rapidly deteriorated, and he died. The 
      autopsy revealed primary pulmonary choriocarcinoma. Early diagnosis of 
      choriocarcinoma based on β-hCG levels in the pleural fluid may be possible.
