TI  - Long-Segment Superior Vena Cava Hypoplasia as an Uncommon Cause of Non-immune 
      Hydrops Fetalis.
PG  - 2258-2261
LID - 10.1007/s00246-025-04013-1 [doi]
AB  - Non-immune hydrops fetalis (NIHF) is a complex perinatal diagnosis with diverse 
      and often idiopathic causes, including impaired lymphatic drainage and 
      compromised venous return. We present the case of a newborn with large bilateral 
      pleural effusions who was subsequently found to have a hypoplastic superior vena 
      cava (SVC). Initially treated with thoracentesis and dietary changes, the 
      infant's symptoms persisted. Follow-up imaging confirmed ongoing SVC narrowing, 
      which was successfully treated with a stent. This case underscores the importance 
      of identifying non-traditional causes of NIHF.
