DP  - 2022
TI  - Diagnosis of non-expandable lung using thoracic ultrasound.
PG  - 101749
LID - 10.1016/j.rmcr.2022.101749 [doi]
LID - 101749
AB  - Non-expandable lung (NEL) commonly occurs secondary to chronic pleural processes, 
      including pleural effusions, endobronchial obstruction, atelectasis, or chronic 
      pleural inflammatory processes. Patients with NEL frequently undergo unnecessary 
      procedures (e.g., thoracentesis), resulting in pneumothorax and discomfort 
      (usually chest pain). Identifying a chronic process and likely development of NEL 
      may prevent this. Diagnostic modalities currently used in practice include 
      pleural manometry and ultrasonography. This case report demonstrates that 
      blunting of transmitted cardiac impulse on M-Mode of ultrasonography predicts the 
      presence of NEL.
