TI  - Sweet hydrothorax: a common presentation of a rare condition.
PG  - 111-114
LID - 10.4103/ajm.AJM_131_18 [doi]
AB  - Sweet hydrothorax is a known, yet rare, complication of peritoneal dialysis. It 
      can be life-threatening. This case is about a 70-year-old lady who presented with 
      acute respiratory failure due to massive right-sided hydrothorax that developed 
      insidiously over 3 months of starting peritoneal dialysis. Thoracentesis and 
      technetium scan confirmed the diagnosis. Treatment was successful with 
      hemodialysis.
