TI  - Left ventricular puncture during thoracentesis.
LID - 10.1136/bcr-2018-227613 [doi]
LID - e227613
AB  - Left ventricular puncture during a thoracentesis is a rare and unusual 
      complication that has yet to be reported. We report a case in which a 74-year-old 
      woman with dilated ischaemic heart disease suffered from puncture of the left 
      ventricle during a routine ultrasound-guided thoracentesis despite following the 
      recommended protocol and procedures. She became haemodynamically unstable and 
      underwent an emergent thoracotomy for removal of the catheter and repair of the 
      left ventricular wall.
