TI  - Recurrent hydrothorax in a child on peritoneal dialysis: A case report and review 
      of the literature.
PG  - 149-151
LID - 10.1002/ccr3.1936 [doi]
AB  - Hydrothorax is a serious complication of peritoneal dialysis, and it may be 
      resolved by deferring dialysis or decreasing dialysate volumes. Repeat 
      thoracentesis is not well tolerated in children. Therefore, if conservative 
      measures fail, thoracotomy or thoracoscopy with endoscopic repair of associated 
      diaphragmatic eventration should be considered before reinstating peritoneal 
      dialysis.
