TI  - Is it possible to standardize the treatment of primary spontaneous pneumothorax? 
      Part 1: etiology, symptoms, diagnostics, minimally invasive treatment.
PG  - 322-327
LID - 10.5114/kitp.2016.64874 [doi]
AB  - The authors of this report present the history of primary spontaneous 
      pneumothorax (PSP) treatment, its etiology, clinical symptoms, and diagnostic 
      methodology. Further, they discuss minimally invasive methods of treating PSP 
      such as thoracentesis and chemical pleurodesis. They discuss the pros and cons of 
      each method, emphasizing that, according to the international recommendations, 
      they should be used as the first line of treatment for PSP.
