TI  - Transudative chylothorax from cirrhosis complicated by lung entrapment.
PG  - 100243
LID - 10.1016/j.rmcr.2015.12.007 [doi]
LID - 100243
AB  - A patient with long-standing cirrhosis due to hepatitis C and hepatic hydrothorax 
      was evaluated for increasing symptoms and presence of a large right pleural 
      effusion. Thoracentesis revealed evidence of a chylothorax with rapid 
      reaccumulation of pleural fluid. Repeat thoracentesis with manometry identified 
      presence of entrapped lung which complicated treatment options. This is the first 
      case report of a hepatic chylothorax with features of entrapped lung.
