TI  - Chest drainage.
PG  - 247-55
LID - 10.1055/s-0032-1330058 [doi]
AB  - Infectious, traumatic, or neoplastic processes in the chest often result in fluid 
      collections within the pleural, parenchymal, or mediastinal spaces. The same 
      fundamental principles that guide drainages of the abdomen can be applied to the 
      chest. This review discusses various pathologic conditions of the thorax that can 
      result in the abnormal accumulation of fluid or air, and their management using 
      image-guided methods.
