DP  - 2013 Mar-Apr
TI  - Thoracic empyema due to migrated gallstones.
PG  - 325-6
AB  - Hepatobiliary conditions should be considered in the differential diagnosis of 
      right pleural effusion. Here we present the illustrative images of thoracic 
      empyema due to migrated gallstones in a woman who was treated for laparoscopic 
      cholecystectomy one year before. The gallstones were obtained unexpectedly during 
      a thoracentesis with aid of an Abrams needle. This rare complication is discussed 
      under current literature review.
