TI  - Cardiac tamponade complicating trimodal therapy for malignant mesothelioma.
PG  - 355-7
AB  - Trimodal therapy, which includes extrapleural pneumonectomy as the cytoreductive 
      procedure followed by combination chemoradiotherapy, is becoming the standard of 
      care in the treatment of malignant mesothelioma. We report here a case of 
      hypotension secondary to tension hydrothorax in which echocardiography and 
      hemodynamic monitoring demonstrated evidence of tamponade physiology. 
      Thoracentesis was lifesaving.
