TI  - Bilateral chylothorax caused by pleuropulmonary lymphangiomyomatosis: a 
      challenging problem in thoracic surgery.
PG  - 151-4
AB  - Massive left-sided pleural effusion in a 35-year-old man was initially diagnosed 
      as idiopathic spontaneous chylothorax and treated with serial thoracenteses and 
      left thoracotomy. Six weeks later, a right thoracotomy was performed for 
      contralateral chylothorax, and histologic examination revealed 
      lymphangiomyomatosis. The patient survived this rare and potentially fatal 
      disease. We have found no previously published case of bilateral 
      lymphangiomyomatosis treated with separate thoracotomies because of bilateral 
      chylothorax.
