TI  - Recurrent unilateral hemorrhagic pleural effusion: A rare manifestation of 
      thoracic endometriosis syndrome.
PG  - 521-523
LID - 10.4103/aca.ACA_17_19 [doi]
AB  - Unilateral recurrent pleural effusions are commonly encountered in critical care 
      practice. Relevant clinical history, physical examination, radiology, and 
      diagnostic thoracentesis usually identify the cause of pleural effusion in most 
      cases. Thoracoscopy or video-assisted thoracic surgery may be required in 
      selective cases. We report a case of 32-year-old female with recurrent unilateral 
      hemorrhagic pleural effusion that was the presenting feature of thoracic 
      endometriosis syndrome.
