TI  - Thoracentesis and thoracic ultrasound: state of the art in 2013.
PG  - 1-9
LID - S0272-5231(12)00123-2 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.ccm.2012.11.005 [doi]
AB  - Thoracentesis is one of the most common medical procedures performed today. With 
      the advent of thoracic ultrasound, thoracentesis has been enhanced with 
      additional preprocedural, intraprocedural, and postprocedural information. The 
      authors review modern-day thoracentesis and the use of ultrasonography. Nearly 
      200,000 thoracenteses are performed among 1.5 million patients with pleural 
      effusion each year. A solid foundation in didactic knowledge and procedural 
      proficiency is important to avoid unwanted complications. Ultrasound has become 
      an indispensable tool to guide performance of thoracentesis. Ultrasonography for 
      this purpose has several advantages. The authors provide a contemporary review on 
      thoracentesis and the use of ultrasonography.
