TI  - Intercostal artery pseudoaneurysm due to thoracentesis: diagnosis with 
      three-dimensional computed tomographic angiography.
PG  - 100-2
LID - 10.1097/RCT.0b013e318243250a [doi]
AB  - Intercostal artery pseudoaneurysm is extremely rare, with only a few case reports 
      in the literature. Presented in this case report is a patient who developed an 
      intercostal artery pseudoaneurysm after thoracentesis for recurrent pleural 
      effusion. Diagnosis traditionally required arteriography; however, as shown in 
      this case, the resolution of current multidetector computed tomography scanners 
      and the routine acquisition of isotropic data sets with 3-dimensional 
      visualization enable identification and detailed characterization of small 
      vascular lesions such as these.
