TI  - Chylothorax in chronic lymphocytic leukemia patient.
PG  - 237-40
AB  - Chronic lymphocytic leukemia (CLL) is rarely complicated by chylothorax: we 
      present a 93-year-old woman with CLL who developed recurrent pleural effusions 
      that were ultimately found to be chylous in nature. Despite eight repeated 
      thoracenteses, she continued to experience re-accumulation of fluid, and 
      therefore, video-assisted thoracotomy with mass ligation of the thoracic duct 
      region plus pleurodesis was performed to resolve the chylothorax. Despite her age 
      and underlying disease, she did well during follow-up. The etiology and 
      management of chylothorax are also reviewed.
