TI  - Congenital pulmonary lymphangiectasia with chylothorax.
PG  - 76-7
AB  - A 5-year-old boy with dyspnea was diagnosed through thoracentesis as having 
      chylothorax. After conservative management failed, open thoracotomy was 
      performed. Lung biopsy confirmed the diagnosis of congenital pulmonary 
      lymphangiectasia. Chylothorax was successfully controlled by fibrin glue 
      pleurodesis in this patient.
