TI  - A case of a thoracic mass negative on thoracentesis diagnosed by cryobiopsy from 
      the visceral pleura.
PG  - e01050
LID - 10.1002/rcr2.1050 [doi]
LID - e01050
AB  - Thoracoscopy under local anaesthesia is recommended for malignant tumours with 
      negative pleural effusion cytology. Cryobiopsy from the visceral pleura by 
      thoracoscopy under local anaesthesia can provide more diagnostic options for 
      patients with thoracentesis-negative malignant effusions. Here we present the 
      first case in which this technique was used. The patient had a pleural metastasis 
      that could not be diagnosed even with rapid cytology of the parietal pleura 
      biopsy. Indications, technical pitfalls, and safety tips are discussed.
