TI  - Splenic Laceration: A Rare Complication of Abdominal Paracentesis.
PG  - e10749
LID - 10.7759/cureus.10749 [doi]
LID - e10749
AB  - Abdominal paracentesis is a commonly performed diagnostic and therapeutic 
      procedure with a low complication rate. Previously described complications 
      include injury to the abdominal wall, small bowel perforation, and abdominal 
      hemorrhage. Splenic injury has also been described as a complication from bedside 
      procedures including colonoscopy, upper gastrointestinal endoscopy, 
      thoracentesis, and pleural biopsy. This case highlights a previously unreported 
      complication from an abdominal paracentesis, splenic laceration.
