TI  - Chylothorax Associated with Chronic Lymphocytic Leukemia.
PG  - 3641-3644
AB  - An 80-year-old man who had suffered from chronic lymphocytic leukemia (CLL) and 
      achieved complete remission was admitted to our hospital due to right pleural 
      effusion. Thoracentesis revealed that the effusion was chyle. Lymphoscintigraphy 
      showed an obstruction of the thoracic duct below the sternum. CD45-gated flow 
      cytometry of the pleural effusion showed elevated numbers of CD5- and 
      CD23-positive lymphocytes and a high serum level of soluble interleukin-2 
      receptor. These results suggested that the chylothorax was caused by the 
      obstruction of the thoracic duct by the sludging of either abnormal lymphocytes 
      of CLL or transformed malignant lymphoma cells.
