TI  - [Thoracentesis under Standing with Assistance of a Tilt Table in Critical 
      Patients after Cardiovascular Surgery].
PG  - 897-900
AB  - For safe and effective drainage in patients with pleural effusion after cardiac 
      surgery, ultrasound-guided thoracocentesis was carried out under standing with 
      assistance of a tilt table. Thoracocentesis was performed in 5( 11%) of the 44 
      patients who were treated under passive orthostatism using a tilt table. Four 
      cases were under intubated-ventilator assist, and 2 cases were under intraaortic 
      balloon pumping( IABP). No adverse events occurred. Thoracocentesis under 
      standing with assistance of a tilt table can be safely performed.
