TI  - Pleural coccidioidomycosis presenting as spontaneous pneumothorax.
LID - bcr-2018-225854 [pii]
LID - 10.1136/bcr-2018-225854 [doi]
LID - bcr2018225854
AB  - Coccidioides is a fungus endemic to Southwestern USA and Northern Mexico which 
      can be asymptomatic or result in a well-defined clinical syndrome of 
      community-acquired pneumonia. On rare occasion, coccidioidomycosis may have 
      atypical presentations as in our patient, a 25-year-old man admitted with a 
      2-month history of progressive dyspnoea and cough. He was found to have a large 
      right-sided pneumothorax with exudative pleural effusion which did not resolve 
      following thoracentesis. Decortication was performed which revealed a dense rind 
      of inflammatory tissue covering all lobes of his right lung. Histopathology 
      demonstrated hyphae resembling Aspergillus, but culture and serology confirmed 
      Coccidioides immitis Following several months of antifungal therapy, he achieved 
      complete clinical recovery with near-complete resolution of radiographic 
      findings.
