TI  - Diffusion-weighted magnetic resonance imaging-directed biopsy of a metastatic 
      bone tumor: Lung adenocarcinoma with ALK rearrangement.
PG  - 170-172
LID - 10.1016/j.rmcr.2018.05.024 [doi]
AB  - A previously healthy 44-year-old Japanese man with a 5-month history of lumbago 
      presented to the emergency department with acute respiratory failure caused by 
      pneumonia, and was immediately intubated. Computed tomography revealed a lung 
      mass, pleural effusion, and multiple osteolytic lesions; however, the results of 
      thoracentesis and bronchial brushing were not definitive. We performed a bone 
      tumor biopsy guided by diffusion-weighted magnetic resonance imaging (DW-MRI) 
      with mechanical ventilation, which enabled the diagnosis of ALK 
      rearrangement-positive lung adenocarcinoma. In the era of precision medicine 
      requiring proper biological tissue collection, DW-MRI was critical for 
      identifying the biopsy site safely and with high precision.
