TI  - Giant left atrium encountered during right-sided thoracentesis.
PG  - 21-22
LID - 10.1016/j.rmcr.2017.11.002 [doi]
AB  - Giant left atrium is an uncommon pathology to encounter during bedside chest 
      ultrasound, but is an important structure to be aware of when considering 
      thoracentesis. This cardiac structure could easily be mistaken for loculated 
      pleural fluid. This case also supports growing evidence that expert users can 
      safely perform thoracentesis without completely reversing therapeutic 
      anticoagulation.
