TI  - Bilateral Chylothorax Complicating a Case of Chronic Lymphocytic Leukemia: A Case 
      Report.
PG  - 951
LID - 10.4081/cp.2017.951 [doi]
LID - 951
AB  - Chylothorax occurs when lymphatic fluid leaks from the thoracic duct and 
      accumulates in the pleural space. Bilateral chylothorax caused by chronic 
      lymphocytic leukemia (CLL) has been rarely reported in the literature. Sludging 
      of lymph might be the underlying cause. We present a case of bilateral 
      chylothorax in a patient with CLL.We also briefly discuss etiology, possible 
      pathogenesis in our case along with diagnostic options and treatment modalities.
