TI  - Nephropleural Fistula Effectively Managed with Serial Thoracentesis: A Case 
      Report.
PG  - 212-214
AB  - Nephropleural fistulae are rare but serious thoracic complications of 
      percutaneous nephrolithotomy (PCNL). Herein, we present the management of a 
      54-year-old female with a delayed presentation of nephropleural fistula. The role 
      of serial thoracentesis as a safe, less invasive, less painful alternative to 
      tube thoracostomy is highlighted. In select cases, this may represent an 
      attractive management strategy for nephropleural fistula after PCNL.
