TI  - Ultrasound for the Pulmonary Consultant.
PG  - 1-9
LID - 10.4137/CCRPM.S33382 [doi]
AB  - Bedside ultrasonographic assessment of the lung and pleura provides rapid, 
      noninvasive, and essential information in diagnosis and management of various 
      pulmonary conditions. Ultrasonography helps in diagnosing common conditions, 
      including consolidation, interstitial syndrome, pleural effusions and masses, 
      pneumothorax, and diaphragmatic dysfunction. It provides procedural guidance for 
      various pulmonary procedures, including thoracentesis, chest tube insertion, 
      transthoracic aspiration, and biopsies. This article describes major applications 
      of ultrasonography for the pulmonary consultant along with illustrative figures 
      and videos.
