TI  - Chemothorax: a rare cause of a transudative pleural effusion.
LID - 10.1136/bcr-2015-212691 [doi]
LID - bcr2015212691
AB  - We discovered a rare cause of pleural effusion, chemothorax. In this case, a 
      patient with invasive ductal breast carcinoma was admitted for a large and 
      symptomatic pleural effusion. The radiology report obtained prior to admission 
      did not describe the location of the Infuse-a-Port catheter. After a bedside 
      thoracentesis demonstrated results consistent with chemotherapy infusate in the 
      pleural space, further review of the medical imaging demonstrated that the 
      catheter was in the pleural space.
