TI  - Extra-lobar Pulmonary Sequestration Requiring Intrauterine Thoracentesis.
PG  - 3
AB  - Congenital lung malformations can result in significant morbidity and mortality 
      in children. Pulmonary sequestration is an uncommon congenital malformation of 
      the lung that can cause complications even in fetal life. We herein present a 
      newborn with extra-lobar sequestration (ELS) that lead to hydrops fetalis 
      necessitating fetal intervention.
