TI  - Hepatic hydrothorax.
PG  - 439-49
LID - S1089-3261(14)00006-3 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.cld.2014.01.005 [doi]
AB  - Hepatic hydrothorax (HH) is an uncommon complication in patients with end-stage 
      liver disease. Only 5% to 10% of patients with end-stage liver disease develop 
      HH, which may result in dyspnea, hypoxia, and infection, and portends a poor 
      prognosis. The most likely explanation for development is passage of fluid from 
      the peritoneal space to the pleural space due to small diaphragmatic defects. 
      Initial management consists of diuretics with dietary sodium restriction and 
      thoracentesis, and a transjugular intrahepatic portosystemic shunt may ultimately 
      be required. Afflicted patients can develop morbid and fatal complications, pose 
      management dilemmas, and should warrant evaluation for liver transplantation.
