TI  - Transjugular intrahepatic portosystemic shunt for treatment of cirrhosis-related 
      chylothorax and chylous ascites: single-institution retrospective experience.
PG  - 992-7
LID - 10.1007/s00270-012-0530-x [doi]
AB  - PURPOSE: To investigate the efficacy and safety of the use of transjugular 
      intrahepatic portosystemic shunt (TIPS) creation to treat cirrhosis-related 
      chylous collections (chylothorax and chylous ascites). METHODS: We 
      retrospectively reviewed data from four patients treated for refractory 
      cirrhosis-related chylous collections with TIPS at our institution over an 8 year 
      period. RESULTS: One patient had chylothorax, and three patients had concomitant 
      chylothorax and chylous ascites. There were no major complications, and the only 
      procedure-related complications occurred in two patients who had mild, treatable 
      hepatic encephalopathy. All patients had improvement as defined by decreased need 
      for thoracentesis or paracentesis, with postprocedure follow-up ranging from 19 
      to 491 days. CONCLUSION: TIPS is a safe procedure that is effective in the 
      treatment of cirrhosis-related chylous collections.
