TI  - Anatomy of the pleura: reflection lines and recesses.
PG  - 165-71, vii
LID - 10.1016/j.thorsurg.2010.12.002 [doi]
AB  - Knowledge of the anatomy of the lines of pleural reflection, triangular 
      ligaments, and pleural recesses is important to thoracic surgeons because their 
      anatomic areas are used daily for radiographic interpretation as well as for the 
      performance of procedures such as chest tube insertion, thoracentesis, and 
      pericardiocentesis. Their knowledge is also important for thoracic surgeons doing 
      surgical procedures such as parietal pleurectomies, extrapleural mobilization and 
      resection of the lungs, and pleuroneumonectomies for destroyed lungs or malignant 
      pleural neoplasms.
