IS  - 2005-6419 (Print)
IS  - 2005-6419 (Linking)
VI  - 59
IP  - 6
DP  - 2010 Dec
TI  - Tension pneumothorax in a newborn after Cesarean-section delivery -A case 
      report-.
PG  - 420-4
LID - 10.4097/kjae.2010.59.6.420 [doi]
AB  - Tension pneumothorax in newborns is a rare but life-threatening complication. We 
      encountered a case of a full-term neonate with a breech presentation. An elective 
      cesarean section was scheduled. Immediately after delivery, the newborn was found 
      to be breathless with a heart rate <60/min. During intubation and cardiac 
      massage, the patient's femoral artery and vein were accessed. The infantogram 
      revealed a right side tension pneumothorax. A 22 gauge needle thoracentesis 
      relieved the right side chest pressure and a closed thoracostomy was performed. 
      The severe acidosis was corrected with sodium bicarbonate. The patient was 
      managed in the neonatal intensive care unit, but died from uncorrectable 
      acidosis. We report this case with a review of the relevant literature.
