TI  - Paragonimiasis presenting with unilateral pseudochylothorax: case report and 
      literature review.
PG  - 386-8
AB  - A 64-y-old female previously treated for lung fluke presented with shortness of 
      breath and moderate left pleural effusion. Thoracentesis was performed and milky 
      pleural effusion was obtained. Paragonimus ova and rhomboidal cholesterol 
      crystals were found. Paragonimiasis was diagnosed, and the patient was treated 
      with praziquantel 25 mg/kg/d.
