TI  - [A case of bilateral chylothorax following neck massage].
PG  - 1034-6
AB  - We report a case of bilateral chylothorax following neck massage. The patient 
      presented with the left supraclavicular mass and bilateral pleural effusions. 
      Both fluids obtained from thoracentesis revealed chylous and a high triglycerides 
      content. The effusions decreased after conservative treatment. Bilateral 
      chylothorax caused by neck massage has, to our knowledge, not previously been 
      reported in literature. We concluded that physicians and massagists should 
      remember this serious complication.
